    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG are delighted to present 95 Silloge Gardens to the market, a spacious three bedroom, two bathroom end of terrace home. Built in the late 1960s, the property extends to approximately 90 sq.m. and benefits from a gas fired central heating system. The property offers well proportioned accommodation throughout, making it an ideal choice for first time buyers, families and those seeking a home with generous living space.\n\nThe accommodation comprises a welcoming entrance hallway, a convenient downstairs WC and a large open plan living and dining room featuring a fireplace, with views overlooking the front and rear gardens. To the rear, the kitchen is fitted with contemporary cabinetry, tiled flooring and a door providing direct access to the rear garden. Upstairs, there are three double bedrooms, including a generous main bedroom overlooking the rear garden and a second bedroom with fitted wardrobes. A fully tiled family shower room completes the accommodation. The property also benefits from a front and rear entrance.\n\nSilloge Gardens is situated in a well established residential area of Ballymun, with a range of local shops, schools and everyday amenities nearby. The property is conveniently located for access to the M50 and M1 motorways, while Dublin City Centre and Dublin Airport are accessible via the local road network. Dublin Bus services also operate in the surrounding area, providing connections to the city centre and neighbouring districts."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nPorch - 1.02m x 2.00m\nGlass enclosed porch to the front of the property, featuring a sliding door which leads to the main entrance door.\n\nEntrance Hall - 3.60m x 3.18m\nBright and welcoming entrance hallway with access to the ground floor accommodation. The hallway leads to the spacious living and dining room and the downstairs WC.\n\nWC - 0.93m x 1.43m\nConveniently located off the entrance hallway, the downstairs WC is fully tiled and comprises a WC and wash hand basin.\n\nLiving/Dining Room - 7.43m x 3.62m\nGenerously proportioned open plan living and dining room, featuring a fireplace as the focal point of the living area. The room extends from the front to the rear of the property, with views overlooking both the front and rear gardens.\n\nKitchen - 3.74m x 2.29m\nPositioned to the rear of the property, the kitchen features sleek, contemporary fitted cabinetry and tiled flooring. A rear door provides convenient access to the rear garden.\n\nLanding - 2.64m x 3.18m\nCarpeted landing with a wooden banister, providing access to all three bedrooms and the family shower room.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.66m x 3.18m\nLarge double bedroom overlooking the rear garden, offering ample space for bedroom furnishings.\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.57m x 2.73m\nSpacious, elongated double bedroom featuring fitted wardrobes, providing useful built in storage.\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.86m x 3.74m\nWell proportioned double bedroom positioned to the front of the property, overlooking the front garden.\n\nShower Room - 1.81m x 2.17m\nFully tiled shower room comprising a shower, WC and wash hand basin.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> 3 Bed, 2 Bath Home</li><li> End of terrace</li><li> Built in the late 1960's</li><li> Approx 90 SQ.M</li><li> Gas Fired central heating</li><li> Front and rear entrance</li><li> BER: F</li><li> Conveniently located close to a range of local amenities, schools and shops, with excellent access to the M50 and M1 motorways, Dublin Airport and regular Dublin Bus services providing links to Dublin City Centre.</ul>"
      },
